' Godot signal handlers + connecting in Bust (Godot slice 5).
'
' Slice 3 declared (`Signal`) and fired (`Emit`) signals; this closes the loop:
' `Connect <source>.<Signal> To <Handler>` wires a signal to a handler method
' (`Sub … End Sub`) that Godot calls back. The wiring is explicit — no magic
' name-matching. `source` is `Me` (own signal) or a `GetNode` handle.
'
' The Emitter pings once a second; the Listener connects to it and prints each
' ping. Lowers to gdext `#[func]` handlers + a string-based `connect(…)`.

Node2D "Emitter"
    Signal Pinged(count As Long)

    Dim elapsed As Single = 0
    Dim count As Long = 0

    On Process(delta)
        elapsed = elapsed + delta
        If elapsed >= 1.0 Then
            elapsed = 0
            count = count + 1
            Emit Pinged(count)
        End If
    End Process
End Node2D

Node2D "Listener"
    On Ready
        Dim emitter As Emitter = Me.GetNode("Emitter")
        Connect emitter.Pinged To OnPinged
    End Ready

    Sub OnPinged(count As Long)
        Debug.Print "listener heard ping " & count
    End Sub
End Node2D
